        "cnm_158"
      ],
      "explanation": "At an intersection, both formulas must be defined and give the same \\(y\\)-value. The denominator of the first formula requires \\(x\\ne2\\). For these allowed inputs,\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}\n=\\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{x-2}\n=x+2.\n\\]\nThus an intersection would require \\(x+2=2x\\), giving \\(x=2\\). But that input makes the original denominator zero, so it cannot give an intersection. The graphs have \\(\\boxed{\\text{no points in common, choice C}}\\).",
